   "notes": "Drawn as a top view of the DIP-4: notch and pin-1 dot at top-left, so pin 1 = A, 2 = K, 3 = E, 4 = C \u2014 matching PC817/4N25/4N35. Input side (A, K) is left of the dashed isolation line, isolated output side (C, E) is right of it; the dashed line is the galvanic barrier and is the whole reason this part is preferred for Q1. Nothing here is at mains potential \u2014 both sides are low-voltage (ESP32 3V3 side and the coin-cell fob side), so no mains red is used. Pin names and destinations follow hardware/schematic/WIRING.md \u00a7 Optocoupler version. Leads run out to x=8 and x=112 so wires attach clear of the body."
